      "observed": "FCC2 VCAP pins 48 and 73 are connected to UART3_FCC2 connector pins 3 and 4, not to decoupling capacitors. The 2u2 capacitors C59 and C67 are instead connected to PH0/unconnected nets rather than the VCAP pins.",
      "expected": "STM32H7 VCAP pins require external decoupling capacitors to GND and should not be merged with UART connector signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"NET0005\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"Pin_3\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"NET0089\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Pin_4\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU core regulator is not properly decoupled and UART/VCAP nets are bridged, risking unstable core supply or damage to the MCU/UART interface.",
      "confidence": 0.90
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows fatal connectivity deviations: the 3V3 supply is not connected to the MCU VDD pins, the HSE crystals are not connected to MCU oscillator pins, and FCC VCAP pins are bridged to a UART connector."
}

